  "description": "Curated reference for Predictive Processing / predictive coding (Rao & Ballard 1999; Friston 2005, 2010; Clark 2013, 2016; Hohwy 2013; Seth 2013, 2021). The brain is treated as a hierarchical generative model that predicts its own sensory inputs and updates only on precision-weighted prediction errors. Includes canonical microcircuit (Bastos et al. 2012), active-inference action branch, controlled-hallucination perception, attention-as-precision, interoceptive inference, conservative vs. radical variants, and critiques (Macpherson, Kogo, Williams).",
